
# Zulihe SHAP Analysis Repository

## Study
Terracing enhances landscape ecological resilience
through erosion reduction on China's Loess Plateau.

## Purpose
This repository provides the R scripts and input
data required to reproduce the SHAP feature
importance analysis and summary visualization.

## Data
The input file contains model-derived SHAP values
and corresponding predictor values.

## Variables
- Feature: Predictor name
- SHAP_value: Model-derived SHAP contribution
- Feature_value: Corresponding predictor value

## Software
R (version 4.3 or later)

Required packages:
- ggplot2
- dplyr
- readr
- patchwork
- scales

## Reproducibility
Run Scripts/01_SHAP_Analysis.R from the
repository root directory.

The script generates:
- Figure4_SHAP.tiff
- Figure4_SHAP.pdf
- SHAP_Global_Importance.csv

## Data integrity
All input values must originate from the actual
study data and fitted model. No simulated or
artificial observations are included.

